{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfP4WUPtQY88ab3m3QpzU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Marta had kept the Skerry light for eleven years, and she knew its moods like a sister's. Each dusk she climbed the a hundred and twelve steps, trimmed the wick, and wound the clockwork that turned the great lens.\n\nOne November night, the fog came in thick as wool. Marta lit the lamp and rang the bell. Far out, she heard a horn answer, faint and wrong. It was a ship, and it was too close to the rocks.\n\nShe rang the bell harder. She swung a lantern from the gallery. The horn came nearer, then turned, and she heard the slow churn of a hull that had found deep water.\n\nAt dawn the fog lifted. A small fishing boat lay at anchor in the cove, its crew asleep on deck. A boy of about ten waved at her from the bow. He held up a fish as long as his arm.\n\nMarta laughed, the first time in weeks. She went down to the kitchen and made tea. Then she went back up and polished the lens until the morning sun made rainbows on the walls.\n\nThat night, she lit the lamp again."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15879,"cache_read_input_tokens":8244,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15879},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da4f4994-a4b3-41aa-8efd-f60ba2a335ef","uuid":"673c06a6-fb9e-4b8f-966f-fcd9008354a6","timestamp":"2026-09-24T22:34:34.674Z","request_id":"req_011CfP4WTyq9ZRFLHB59fD9i"}
